course: dictionary
lesson: 4226
title: Grainy: rough texture and blurry pictures
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Grainy means having a rough texture with tiny bits in it, like sand or sugar. It can also describe a photo or video that looks spotty because it is not clear.
explain: Use the words around it to check. «Honey that turns hard and grainy has crystallised and is not bad.» The honey is hard and rough, so grainy describes how it feels, and it is not a sign that the honey has gone bad.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. "The old photo was grainy, so we could not see faces clearly" makes sense if grainy means blurry and spotty. If the meaning does not fit, check again.
fact: Grainy means having a rough texture with small bits or grains in it.
fact: «Honey that turns hard and grainy has crystallised and is not bad.»
fact: A grainy photo or video is not clear and looks spotty, made of tiny dots.
fact: Grainy bread or wood has a visible grain pattern.
fact: Grainy is an adjective, so it can change to grainier and grainiest.
exercise: «Honey that turns hard and grainy has crystallised and is not bad.» What does grainy describe here? | *The rough texture of the honey | The colour of the jar | The smell of the kitchen
exercise: A grainy video makes it hard to see faces. What does grainy mean in this sentence? | *Not clear, spotty, made of tiny dots | Very bright and colourful | Fast and loud
exercise: Which word is the opposite of grainy when we talk about texture? | Sandy | Bumpy | *Smooth | Gritty
test: Grainy bread has which visible feature? | A glossy coat | A cold, wet surface | *A visible grain pattern
test: In a story, what can a grainy picture be? | A loud sound | *A clue that is hard to read | A map of the sea
exam: Which sentence uses grainy correctly? | She grainy the bread with a loud song. | The bright sunny sky was grainy and warm. | *The old security video was so grainy that we could not tell who was walking in.
